                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca3ebd28-259d-45e0-933e-7e4d8f65ca82",
                                "sense_id": "6370f795-d829-3ffe-a5bc-8c6db64e1d89",
                                "text": "Stara nauczycielka wyszukiwała potulne ofiary wśród swoich uczniów."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f4ba686a-ffd2-4575-bc2c-4069faad46ab",
                        "source_entry_id": "e9482764-84bf-3bb1-8233-b40ab1def8a5",
                        "source_sense_id": "6370f795-d829-3ffe-a5bc-8c6db64e1d89",
                        "target_lang_word": "docile",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "docile",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c702ccac-4a5e-36cd-b1d4-bd71d74880cb",
                                        "entry_id": "712e44ae-5a10-3d0e-bab7-a640be02129a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ready to accept instruction or direction; obedient; subservient."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc9ea809-41b0-465a-9bcc-a64e914c3d10",
                                                "sense_id": "c702ccac-4a5e-36cd-b1d4-bd71d74880cb",
                                                "text": "With that he dropped his head again, lamenting over and caressing her, and there was not a sound in all the house for a long, long time; they remaining clasped in one another’s arms, in the glorious sunshine that had crept in with Florence.\nHe dressed himself for going out, with a docile submission to her entreaty; and walking with a feeble gait, and looking back, with a tremble, at the room in which he had been so long shut up, and where he had seen the picture in the glass, passed out with her into the hall."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e9f94d5-c350-49a7-bbb2-9a982cffbf68",
                                                "sense_id": "c702ccac-4a5e-36cd-b1d4-bd71d74880cb",
                                                "text": "Harriet certainly was not clever, but she had a sweet, docile, grateful disposition; was totally free from conceit; and only desiring to be guided by any one she looked up to."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cca5db22-62b8-30b7-ab41-bc7bcc099597",
                                        "entry_id": "712e44ae-5a10-3d0e-bab7-a640be02129a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Yielding to control or supervision, direction, or management."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8fa581da-fc96-4f2f-a13f-81324e22c679",
                                                "sense_id": "cca5db22-62b8-30b7-ab41-bc7bcc099597",
                                                "text": "Such literature may well be anathema to those, who are too docile and petty for their own good."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ce4b11fc-51e6-4181-875c-39e984ccf629",
                        "source_entry_id": "e9482764-84bf-3bb1-8233-b40ab1def8a5",
                        "source_sense_id": "6370f795-d829-3ffe-a5bc-8c6db64e1d89",
                        "target_lang_word": "meek",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "meek",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dcd891cc-7cad-3a4c-a847-4b03dd702eee",
                                        "entry_id": "8c1fa107-9865-3b2a-96d6-625131cf8888",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Humble, non-boastful, modest, meager, or self-effacing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb5f0bc7-907b-468a-b37e-7d5b025b5a01",
                                                "sense_id": "dcd891cc-7cad-3a4c-a847-4b03dd702eee",
                                                "text": "Blessed are the meeke: for they shall inherit the earth."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "667d63c4-e3bd-4331-85de-fb071723bbf8",
                                                "sense_id": "dcd891cc-7cad-3a4c-a847-4b03dd702eee",
                                                "text": "Mrs. Wickam was a meek woman...who was always ready to pity herself, or to be pitied, or to pity anybody else..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e9b64fa9-1354-3d11-9a36-8f1ce11cd98b",
                                        "entry_id": "8c1fa107-9865-3b2a-96d6-625131cf8888",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Submissive, dispirited, cowed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "abd7fcfd-d773-4c47-93bf-a93bb1bdbcd7",
                                                "sense_id": "e9b64fa9-1354-3d11-9a36-8f1ce11cd98b",
                                                "text": "What if they were wolves instead of lambs? They'd eat her all the sooner if she was meek to them. Fight or be eaten."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
